From 7a0d64fcab836c393537bbfdd065a6109e6affb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:50:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nl: report netlink errors back to the caller

bridge_nl_error_cb() is installed as the NL_CB_CUSTOM error handler and
returns NL_SKIP on every path, so libnl treats the error message as
consumed and nl_wait_for_ack() returns 0: every rejected request looks
like a success to the caller.

bridger_nl_flow_offload_add() depends on that return value. It walks the
device's offload chain and stops at the first device that accepts the
flower filter. On a MediaTek MT7988 board with a Motorcomm YT9224 switch
the DSA user port rejects the skip_sw filter with -EOPNOTSUPP - that
switch offloads ACL rules, not a redirect to a Wi-Fi netdev - but the
error was swallowed, so bridger recorded the flow as offloaded and never
tried the conduit, where the MediaTek PPE accepts the very same rule.

Return NL_STOP instead, which makes libnl return
-nl_syserr2nlerr(err->error), as its default error handler does. The
error then reaches the caller, which falls back to the next device:

  Add flow on lan1: No child process   (strerror of NLE_OPNOTSUPP)
  Add flow on eth1: Success

With that, a LAN to Wi-Fi transfer on this board is offloaded in both
directions - the ingress and egress netdev counters stay at zero while
the Wi-Fi station counters keep rising - instead of being forwarded by
the CPU.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
---
 nl.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nl.c b/nl.c
index f326d8e..f11857f 100644
--- a/nl.c
+++ b/nl.c
@@ -1030,7 +1030,7 @@ bridge_nl_error_cb(struct sockaddr_nl *nla, struct nlmsgerr *err,
 		return NL_SKIP;
 
 	if (!(nlh->nlmsg_flags & NLM_F_ACK_TLVS))
-		return NL_SKIP;
+		return NL_STOP;
 
 	if (!(nlh->nlmsg_flags & NLM_F_CAPPED))
 		ack_len += err->msg.nlmsg_len - sizeof(*nlh);
@@ -1044,7 +1044,7 @@ bridge_nl_error_cb(struct sockaddr_nl *nla, struct nlmsgerr *err,
 
 	D("Netlink error(%d): %s\n", err->error, errstr);
 
-	return NL_SKIP;
+	return NL_STOP;
 }
 
 struct nl_sock *
-- 
2.55.0

